    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0440" n="1904" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p2/pg1904"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690D.91/11–1651: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in India</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New Delhi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-11-16T19:00:00+05:30">November 16,
                            1951—7 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1770. Have just completed calls on all Chiefs of Mission, and in the course of
                    each conversation I asked for an opinion on who wld win honest and uninfluenced
                    plebiscite in Kashmir. Each without exception stated that India wld win; margins
                    varied from three to two to four to one. Many of these mission chiefs or their
                    staffs visited <pb facs="0441" n="1905" xml:id="pg1905"/> Kashmir recently. Amer
                    press here, several of whom have recently visited Kashmir, also agree with this
                    analysis.</p>
                <p>Emb estimates are more modest as to margin but no disagreement over likelihood
                    that India wld win under conditions likely to prevail.</p>
                <p>Much of India’s improved position undoubtedly due to Sheik Abdullah’s land and
                    tax reforms which have won much support among peasants.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
